# SPECTRE // OBSIDIAN

A local-first, read-only system and network intelligence dashboard for Windows.

**Start here:** [OBSIDIAN-README.md](OBSIDIAN-README.md)

The **Obsidian** interface is a new responsive, browser-rendered dashboard, backed by the original Python monitoring engine. The previous PySide6 frontend is retained in `src/ghost/app.py` but is no longer the default launcher.

### Quick start (Windows)

Run `scripts\run_obsidian.bat` from the extracted project. To build an executable, run `scripts\build_windows.bat`, then launch `dist\SPECTRE-OBSIDIAN.exe`.

The application runs a local HTTP server on `127.0.0.1`, opens the dashboard in your browser, and stops when you close the console. No cloud account or external assets required.

### Features

CPU, RAM, disk and NVIDIA GPU telemetry; network traffic history; live connection inventory; process and listener tables; live security advisories; local SQLite history; CSV export; DNS and ping diagnostics. Connection filters and sorting remain in place during live updates.

**Security:** Observations are not malware verdicts. SPECTRE does not scan, block, or modify network connections.
